// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`the Introduction: write, reject with a point, fix, accept each tier reads its own brief, and the task ends Accepted: writer brief, attempt 1 1`] = `
"work brief a2 · writer (low) · t1 The Introduction · attempt 1 of 3
snapshot: tsd-writing@1
project: <project> (run every work command in this folder)

YOU ARE  low tier. You execute one unit of work, report it, and stop.
ROLE     Writes one TSD region from its brief.
         - Write the region under its heading in the file that WORK IN names.
         - Report it with work report as docs/tsd.md#introduction.
TASK     Write the Introduction from the agreed facts.
WORK IN  docs/tsd.md (source tsd); verify: work-lint docs/tsd.md (run it in the project folder; exit 0 = ready)
READ     docs/facts.md#dedupe
RULES    no-code-proof  No file paths with line numbers, no commit hashes in the body  (linter)
         no-ticket-ids  No ticket ids and no chat-thread citations  (linter)
         repeatable     A reviewer can repeat the problem without the design  (region-lead)

YOUR TURN
  report   work report a2.k0002 --output=docs/tsd.md#introduction
           If WORK IN names a verify command, run it first; exit 0 means ready. If it fails and you cannot fix it, raise with its output.
  raise    work raise a2.k0002 --reason="<the missing fact, and where you looked>"
           Raise when the brief is not enough to do the work. Do not guess.
  suggest  work suggest a2.k0002 <rule id> --says="<why it cannot be met, with the fact>"
           The rule stays until an official draft answers the suggestion; raise if you cannot continue.
STOP after one report or one raise. Do not run other work commands."
`;

exports[`the Introduction: write, reject with a point, fix, accept each tier reads its own brief, and the task ends Accepted: linter brief on r1 1`] = `
"work brief a3 · linter (low) · t1 The Introduction
snapshot: tsd-writing@1
project: <project> (run every work command in this folder)

YOU ARE  low tier. You execute one unit of work, report it, and stop.
ROLE     Checks one region against the rules in its checks.
         - Give one --evidence line for each rule in your checks.
         - Reject with one --point for each rule that the region breaks.
TASK     the maker's task (you check it; you do not do it): Write the Introduction from the agreed facts.
WORK IN  docs/tsd.md (source tsd)
READ     docs/facts.md#dedupe
CHECKS   no-code-proof  No file paths with line numbers, no commit hashes in the body  (linter)
         no-ticket-ids  No ticket ids and no chat-thread citations  (linter)
REVIEW   r1 by a2 (writer): docs/tsd.md#introduction
OPEN     no evidence on r1 for no-code-proof (checked by linter)
         no evidence on r1 for no-ticket-ids (checked by linter)

YOUR TURN
  accept   work review a3.k0003 r1 accept --evidence="no-code-proof | <where you looked in docs/tsd.md#introduction> | <what you saw>" --evidence="no-ticket-ids | <where you looked in docs/tsd.md#introduction> | <what you saw>"
           One --evidence line for each rule in your checks, with where you looked and what you saw in a sentence of words. Accept only when every rule holds.
  reject   work review a3.k0003 r1 reject --point="<what is wrong, and where>" --breaks=<rule id>
           One --point for each problem. Name the rule that it breaks; leave --breaks out if no rule covers it.
  raise    work raise a3.k0003 --reason="<the missing fact, and where you looked>"
           Raise when the brief is not enough to do the work. Do not guess.
  suggest  work suggest a3.k0003 <rule id> --says="<why it cannot be met, with the fact>"
           The rule stays until an official draft answers the suggestion; raise if you cannot continue.
STOP after one review or one raise. Do not run other work commands."
`;

